<!-- Challenges and Customization -->
<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-4">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 me-3 p-3" alt="Banking Applications" /></div>
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/woman-tech-desk-chart-bureau.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Banking Applications" /></div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-8 Imgborder" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Banking Applications Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>
                <p>Financial organizations can face disconnected systems, manual processes, inconsistent customer journeys, limited visibility and operational complexity.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Disconnected Financial Systems:</b> Connect banking, CRM, payment, loan, accounting and reporting systems through integrated workflows.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Manual Financial Processes:</b> Automate repetitive data entry, approvals, notifications, reconciliation and routine operational activities.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Limited Financial Visibility:</b> Use centralized dashboards and reports to provide timely insights into financial and operational performance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Complex Customer Journeys:</b> Create consistent digital experiences across banking, payments, loans, customer service and other financial touchpoints.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Security and Data Concerns:</b> Use structured access controls, secure integrations and appropriate financial data-management practices.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />

                <h3><b>The Importance of Customization in Banking Applications</b></h3>
                <p>Every financial organization has different products, policies, customers, processes and business rules. Customization helps the solution fit the company's operating model.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Customize Financial Workflows:</b> Configure banking applications processes around the organization's actual financial policies, products and operating model.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Create Role-Based Experiences:</b> Give customers, financial staff, managers and administrators the information and actions relevant to their roles.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Automate Notifications:</b> Configure alerts, reminders, approvals and workflow notifications for important financial events.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Build Custom Dashboards:</b> Provide role-specific reporting and visibility into important financial and operational indicators.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  <b>Use Customer and User Feedback:</b> Continuously improve the solution based on real-world usage, feedback and measurable business outcomes.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

